  "content" : "# Follo.Money (Follo)\n\n### Follow the money\n\nFund politics, and see how funding is used.\n\n1. Campaigns say how much they need, over time. \n2. People donate to campaigns. \n3. Everyone can see expenditures transparently. \n\n### How it works:\n- Anyone can create a campaign by giving it a name and a timed initial spending limit.\n- People donate to campaigns, knowing the campaign cant use more than what they’ve agreed to, for the specified amount of time.\n- Donors keep access to a portion of a campaign's surplus funds. \n- Keep in mind a campaign can change its spending after the initial limit’s duration, all surplus funds become accessible, the owner decides if and when to set another timed spending limit.\n\n### Why it works:\n- The public sector doesn’t benefit from private transactions. Winning politicians are doing things more transparently, more authentically. \n- People either prefer to be able to see where their money goes, or they're indifferent about it. No one strongly prefers their elected officials keep things from them.\n- The status quo is ActBlue (https://secure.actblue.com/donate/zohran-mamdani-transition-1/). It is a dead simple payment experience.\n- We've finally got the right tools to make this type of thing happen without relying on bankers.\n- The public sector should use efficient payment rails owned by the public sector.\n\n\n### Who's it for:\nZohran. As Zohran continues asking for money, given his politics, he should prefer a system that allows him to be upfront about how much funds are needed, and his movement should prefer transparency and authenticity...\n\n...so long as its also a dead simple experience for donors and campaign owners. The money has to flow.\n\n\n",
